The following images represent the outputs generated from the MATLAB simulations included in this project. The image processing module produces step-by-step results such as the original input image, grayscale conversion, noise-reduced filtered image, detected crack edges using the Canny algorithm, rust segmentation mask, and final overlay images highlighting cracks and rust regions on the original surface. These outputs demonstrate how the algorithm progressively processes the image to identify corrosion and structural defects.

The PID control module generates the “PID Simulation” plot, which shows the yaw response of the submarine and the controller output over time in the presence of disturbances. This graph verifies that the PID controller successfully stabilizes the system and maintains the desired orientation.
